,"page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"✅"},"3196":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-372","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"✅"},"3197":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-373","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"Hadoop-2.5.x"},"3198":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-374","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"❌"},"3199":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-375","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"⚠️"},"3200":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-376","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"✅"},"3201":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-377","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-1x-release-lines","content":"✅"},"3202":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-378","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-pre-10-release-lines","content":"Starting around the time of Hadoop version 2.7.0, the Hadoop PMC got into the habit of calling out\nnew minor releases on their major version 2 release line as not stable / production ready. As\nsuch, HBase expressly advises downstream users to avoid running on top of these releases. Note\nthat additionally the 2.8.1 release was given the same caveat by the Hadoop PMC. For reference,\nsee the release announcements for Apache Hadoop\n2.7.0, Apache Hadoop\n2.8.0, Apache Hadoop\n2.8.1, and Apache Hadoop\n2.9.0."},"3203":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-379","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-pre-10-release-lines","content":"The Hadoop PMC called out the 3.1.0 release as not stable / production ready. As such, HBase\nexpressly advises downstream users to avoid running on top of this release. For reference, see the\nrelease announcement for Hadoop 3.1.0."},"3204":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-380","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-version-support-matrix-for-eom-pre-10-release-lines","content":"Because HBase depends on Hadoop, it bundles Hadoop jars under its *lib* directory. The bundled\njars are ONLY for use in stand-alone mode. In distributed mode, it is *critical* that the version\nof Hadoop that is out on your cluster match what is under HBase. Replace the hadoop jars found in\nthe HBase lib directory with the equivalent hadoop jars from the version you are running on your\ncluster to avoid version mismatch issues. Make sure you replace the jars under HBase across your\nwhole cluster. Hadoop version mismatch issues have various manifestations. Check for mismatch if\nHBase appears hung."},"3205":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-381","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-3-support-for-the-hbase-binary-releases-and-maven-artifacts","content":"For HBase 2.5.1 and earlier, the official HBase binary releases and Maven artifacts were built with Hadoop 2.x."},"3206":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-382","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-3-support-for-the-hbase-binary-releases-and-maven-artifacts","content":"Starting with HBase 2.5.2, HBase provides binary releases and Maven artifacts built with both Hadoop 2.x and Hadoop 3.x. The Hadoop 2 artifacts do not have any version suffix, the Hadoop 3 artifacts add the `-hadoop-3` suffix to the version. i.e. `hbase-2.5.2-bin.tar.gz.asc` is the Binary release built with Hadoop2, and `hbase-2.5.2-hadoop3-bin.tar.gz` is the release built with Hadoop 3."},"3207":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-383","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-3-version-policy","content":"Each HBase release has a default Hadoop 3 version. This is used when the Hadoop 3 version is not specified during build, and for building the official binary releases and artifacts. Generally when a new minor version is released (i.e. 2.5.0) the default version is set to the latest supported Hadoop 3 version at the start of the release process."},"3208":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-384","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-3-version-policy","content":"Up to HBase 2.5.10 and 2.6.1 even if HBase added support for newer Hadoop 3 releases in a patch release, the default Hadoop 3 version (and the one used in the official binary releases) was not updated. This simplified upgrading, but meant that HBase releases often included old unfixed CVEs both from Hadoop and Hadoop's dependencies, even when newer Hadoop releases with fixes were available."},"3209":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-385","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#hadoop-3-version-policy","content":"Starting with HBase 2.5.11 and 2.6.2, the default Hadoop 3 version is always set to the latest supported Hadoop 3 version, and is also used for the `-hadoop3` binary releases and artifacts. This will drastically reduce the number of known CVEs shipped in the HBase binary releases, and make sure that all fixes and improvements in Hadoop are included."},"3210":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-386","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#dfsdatanodemaxtransferthreads","content":"An HDFS DataNode has an upper bound on the number of files that it will serve at any one time. Before doing any loading, make sure you have configured Hadoop's *conf/hdfs-site.xml*, setting the `dfs.datanode.max.transfer.threads` value to at least the following:"},"3211":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-387","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#dfsdatanodemaxtransferthreads","content":"Be sure to restart your HDFS after making the above configuration."},"3212":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-388","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#dfsdatanodemaxtransferthreads","content":"Not having this configuration in place makes for strange-looking failures. One manifestation is a complaint about missing blocks. For example:"},"3213":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-389","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#dfsdatanodemaxtransferthreads","content":"See also Case Studies and note that this property was previously known as `dfs.datanode.max.xcievers` (e.g. Hadoop HDFS: Deceived by Xciever)."},"3214":{"id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites-390","page_id":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/basic-prerequisites#zookeeper-requirements","content":"An Apache ZooKeeper quorum is required. The exact version depends on your version of HBase, though the minimum ZooKeeper version is 3.4.x due to the `useMulti` feature made default in 1.0.0 (see HBASE-16598)."},"3215":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","type":"page","content":"Running and Confirming Your Installation","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Configuration & Setup","Configuration"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/confirm"},"3216":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-0","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Steps to start HBase services and verify your installation is working correctly."},"3217":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-1","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Make sure HDFS is running first. Start and stop the Hadoop HDFS daemons by running *bin/start-hdfs.sh* over in the `HADOOP_HOME` directory. You can ensure it started properly by testing the `put` and `get` of files into the Hadoop filesystem. HBase does not normally use the MapReduce or YARN daemons. These do not need to be started."},"3218":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-2","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"*If* you are managing your own ZooKeeper, start it and confirm it's running, else HBase will start up ZooKeeper for you as part of its start process."},"3219":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-3","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Start HBase with the following command:"},"3220":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-4","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Run the above from the `HBASE_HOME` directory."},"3221":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-5","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"You should now have a running HBase instance. HBase logs can be found in the *logs* subdirectory. Check them out especially if HBase had trouble starting."},"3222":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-6","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"HBase also puts up a UI listing vital attributes. By default it's deployed on the Master host at port 16010 (HBase RegionServers listen on port 16020 by default and put up an informational HTTP server at port 16030). If the Master is running on a host named `master.example.org` on the default port, point your browser at http\\://master.example.org:16010 to see the web interface."},"3223":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-7","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Once HBase has started, see the shell exercises documentation for how to create tables, add data, scan your insertions, and finally disable and drop your tables."},"3224":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-8","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"To stop HBase after exiting the HBase shell enter"},"3225":{"id":"/docs/configuration/confirm-9","page_id":"/docs/configuration/confirm","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/confirm","content":"Shutdown can take a moment to complete. It can take longer if your cluster is comprised of many machines. If you are running a distributed operation, be sure to wait until HBase has shut down completely before stopping the Hadoop daemons."},"3226":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","type":"page","content":"Default Configuration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Configuration & Setup","Configuration"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/default"},"3227":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-0","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/configuration/default","content":"HBase default configuration properties and how to customize them via hbase-site.xml for site-specific settings."},"3228":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-1","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/default#hbase-sitexml-and-hbase-defaultxml","content":"*hbase-site.xml* and *hbase-default.xml*"},"3229":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-2","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/default#configuration-default-hbase-default-configuration","content":"HBase Default configuration"},"3230":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-3","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/default#hbasetmpdir-toc","content":"`hbase.tmp.dir` [!toc]"},"3231":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-4","page_id":"/docs/configuration/default","type":"heading","tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/configuration/default#hbaserootdir-toc","content":"`hbase.rootdir` [!toc]"},"3232":{"id":"/docs/configuration/default-5","page_id":"/d