erver-example","content":"The following Observer coprocessor prevents the details of the user `admin` from being\nreturned in a `Get` or `Scan` of the `users` table."},"4187":{"id":"/docs/cp-128","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Write a class that implements the\nRegionCoprocessor,\nRegionObserver\nclass."},"4188":{"id":"/docs/cp-129","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Override the `preGetOp()` method (the `preGet()` method is deprecated) to check\nwhether the client has queried for the rowkey with value `admin`. If so, return an\nempty result. Otherwise, process the request as normal."},"4189":{"id":"/docs/cp-130","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Put your code and dependencies in a JAR file."},"4190":{"id":"/docs/cp-131","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Place the JAR in HDFS where HBase can locate it."},"4191":{"id":"/docs/cp-132","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Load the Coprocessor."},"4192":{"id":"/docs/cp-133","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Write a simple program to test it."},"4193":{"id":"/docs/cp-134","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Following are the implementation of the above steps:"},"4194":{"id":"/docs/cp-135","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"Overriding the `preGetOp()` will only work for `Get` operations. You also need to override\nthe `preScannerOpen()` method to filter the `admin` row from scan results."},"4195":{"id":"/docs/cp-136","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#observer-example","content":"This method works but there is a *side effect*. If the client has used a filter in\nits scan, that filter will be replaced by this filter. Instead, you can explicitly\nremove any `admin` results from the scan:"},"4196":{"id":"/docs/cp-137","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Still using the `users` table, this example implements a coprocessor to calculate\nthe sum of all employee salaries, using an endpoint coprocessor."},"4197":{"id":"/docs/cp-138","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Create a '.proto' file defining your service."},"4198":{"id":"/docs/cp-139","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Execute the `protoc` command to generate the Java code from the above .proto' file."},"4199":{"id":"/docs/cp-140","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"This will generate a class call `Sum.java`."},"4200":{"id":"/docs/cp-141","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Write a class that extends the generated service class, implement the `Coprocessor`\nand `CoprocessorService` classes, and override the service method."},"4201":{"id":"/docs/cp-142","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"If you load a coprocessor from `hbase-site.xml` and then load the same coprocessor\nagain using HBase Shell, it will be loaded a second time. The same class will\nexist twice, and the second instance will have a higher ID (and thus a lower priority).\nThe effect is that the duplicate coprocessor is effectively ignored."},"4202":{"id":"/docs/cp-143","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Load the Coprocessor."},"4203":{"id":"/docs/cp-144","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#endpoint-example","content":"Write a client code to call the Coprocessor."},"4204":{"id":"/docs/cp-145","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"**Bundling Coprocessors**\\\nYou can bundle all classes for a coprocessor into a\nsingle JAR on the RegionServer's classpath, for easy deployment. Otherwise,\nplace all dependencies on the RegionServer's classpath so that they can be\nloaded during RegionServer start-up. The classpath for a RegionServer is set\nin the RegionServer's `hbase-env.sh` file."},"4205":{"id":"/docs/cp-146","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"**Automating Deployment**\\\nYou can use a tool such as Puppet, Chef, or\nAnsible to ship the JAR for the coprocessor to the required location on your\nRegionServers' filesystems and restart each RegionServer, to automate\ncoprocessor deployment. Details for such set-ups are out of scope of this\ndocument."},"4206":{"id":"/docs/cp-147","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"**Updating a Coprocessor**\\\nDeploying a new version of a given coprocessor is not as simple as disabling it,\nreplacing the JAR, and re-enabling the coprocessor. This is because you cannot\nreload a class in a JVM unless you delete all the current references to it.\nSince the current JVM has reference to the existing coprocessor, you must restart\nthe JVM, by restarting the RegionServer, in order to replace it. This behavior\nis not expected to change."},"4207":{"id":"/docs/cp-148","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"**Coprocessor Logging**\\\nThe Coprocessor framework does not provide an API for logging beyond standard Java\nlogging."},"4208":{"id":"/docs/cp-149","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"**Coprocessor Configuration**\\\nIf you do not want to load coprocessors from the HBase Shell, you can add their configuration\nproperties to `hbase-site.xml`. In Using HBase Shell, two arguments are\nset: `arg1=1,arg2=2`. These could have been added to `hbase-site.xml` as follows:"},"4209":{"id":"/docs/cp-150","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#guidelines-for-deploying-a-coprocessor","content":"Then you can read the configuration using code like the following:"},"4210":{"id":"/docs/cp-151","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"Restricting arbitrary user coprocessors can be a big concern in multitenant environments. HBase provides a continuum of options for ensuring only expected coprocessors are running:"},"4211":{"id":"/docs/cp-152","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.enabled`: Enables or disables all coprocessors. This will limit the functionality of HBase, as disabling all coprocessors will disable some security providers. An example coproccessor so affected is `org.apache.hadoop.hbase.security.access.AccessController`."},"4212":{"id":"/docs/cp-153","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.user.enabled`: Enables or disables loading coprocessors on tables (i.e. user coprocessors)."},"4213":{"id":"/docs/cp-154","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"One can statically load coprocessors, and optionally tune their priorities, via the following tunables in `hbase-site.xml`:"},"4214":{"id":"/docs/cp-155","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.regionserver.classes`: A comma-separated list of coprocessors that are loaded by region servers"},"4215":{"id":"/docs/cp-156","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.region.classes`: A comma-separated list of RegionObserver and Endpoint coprocessors"},"4216":{"id":"/docs/cp-157","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.user.region.classes`: A comma-separated list of coprocessors that are loaded by all regions"},"4217":{"id":"/docs/cp-158","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.master.classes`: A comma-separated list of coprocessors that are loaded by the master (MasterObserver coprocessors)"},"4218":{"id":"/docs/cp-159","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.wal.classes`: A comma-separated list of WALObserver coprocessors to load"},"4219":{"id":"/docs/cp-160","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.abortonerror`: Whether to abort the daemon which has loaded the coprocessor if the coprocessor should error other than `IOError`. If this is set to false and an access controller coprocessor should have a fatal error the coprocessor will be circumvented, as such in secure installations this is advised to be `true`; however, one may override this on a per-table basis for user coprocessors, to ensure they do not abort their running region server and are instead unloaded on error."},"4220":{"id":"/docs/cp-161","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`hbase.coprocessor.region.whitelist.paths`: A comma separated list available for those loading `org.apache.hadoop.hbase.security.access.CoprocessorWhitelistMasterObserver` whereby one can use the following options to white-list paths from which coprocessors may be loaded."},"4221":{"id":"/docs/cp-162","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"Coprocessors on the classpath are implicitly white-listed"},"4222":{"id":"/docs/cp-163","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"`*` to wildcard all coprocessor paths"},"4223":{"id":"/docs/cp-164","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"An entire filesystem (e.g. `hdfs://my-cluster/`)"},"4224":{"id":"/docs/cp-165","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"A wildcard path to be evaluated by FilenameUtils.wildcardMatch"},"4225":{"id":"/docs/cp-166","page_id":"/docs/cp","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/cp#restricting-coprocessor-usage","content":"Note: Path can specify scheme or not (e.g. `file:///usr/hbase/lib/coprocessors` or for all filesystems `/usr/hbase/lib/coprocessors`)"},"4226":{"id":"/docs/datamodel","page_id":"/docs/datamodel","type":"page","content":"Data Model","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Core Concepts"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/datamodel"},"4227":{"id":"/docs/datamodel-0","page_id":"/docs/datamodel","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/datamodel","content":"In HBase, data is stored in tables, which have rows and columns. This is a terminology overlap with relational databases (RDBMSs), but this is not a helpful analogy. Instead, it can be helpful to think of an HBase table as a multi-dimensional map."},"4228":{"id":"/docs/datamodel-1","page_id":"/docs/