endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`GET`"},"4609":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-196","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"Scanning with a filter `PrefixFilter('row1')`. The filter should be specified according to the Thrift Filter Language and then encoded as `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` MIME format string."},"4610":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-197","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`/table/*?filter_b64=b64_encoded_filter`"},"4611":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-198","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`GET`"},"4612":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-199","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"Scanning with a filter `PrefixFilter('row1')`. The filter should be specified according to the Thrift Filter Language and then encoded in URL-safe base64."},"4613":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-200","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"**Examples:**"},"4614":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-201","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"The stateful scanner API expects clients to restart scans if there is a REST server failure in the midst. The stateless does not store any state related to scan operation and all the parameters are specified as query parameters."},"4615":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-202","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"The stateless endpoints are optimized for small results, while the stateful scanner\nAPI can also be used for large\nresults."},"4616":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-203","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"The following are the scan parameters:"},"4617":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-204","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`startrow` - The start row for the scan."},"4618":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-205","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`endrow` - The end row for the scan."},"4619":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-206","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`column` - The comma separated list of columns to scan."},"4620":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-207","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`starttime`, `endtime` - To only retrieve columns within a specific range of version timestamps, both start and end time must be specified."},"4621":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-208","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`maxversions` - To limit the number of versions of each column to be returned."},"4622":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-209","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`batchsize` - To limit the maximum number of values returned for each call to next()."},"4623":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-210","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`limit` - The number of rows to return in the scan operation."},"4624":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-211","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`cacheblocks` - Whether to use the Block Cache in the RegionServer. By default `true`."},"4625":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-212","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`reversed` - When set to `true`, reverse scan will be executed. By default `false`."},"4626":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-213","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`filter` - Allows to specify a filter for the scan as an `application/x-www-form-urlencoded` MIME format string."},"4627":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-214","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`filter_b64` - On versions which include the HBASE-28518 patch, `filter_b64` allows to specify a URL-safe base64 encoded filter for the scan. When both `filter` and `filter_b64` are specified, only `filter_b64` is considered."},"4628":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-215","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`includeStartRow` - Whether start row should be included in the scan. By default `true`."},"4629":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-216","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`includeStopRow` - Whether end row (stop row) should be included in the scan. By default `false`."},"4630":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-217","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"`includeStartRow` and `includeStopRow` are only supported on versions that include HBASE-28627."},"4631":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-218","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"Versions without this patch will either ignore these parameters or will error out if they are set to a non-default value."},"4632":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-219","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"More on start row, end row and limit parameters:"},"4633":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-220","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"If start row, end row and limit not specified, then the whole table will be scanned."},"4634":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-221","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"If start row and limit (say N) is specified, then the scan operation will return N rows from the start row specified."},"4635":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-222","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"If only limit parameter is specified, then the scan operation will return N rows from the start of the table."},"4636":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-223","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"If limit and end row are specified, then the scan operation will return N rows from start of table till the end row. If the end row is reached before N rows ( say M and M \\< N ), then M rows will be returned to the user."},"4637":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-224","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#stateless-endpoints-for-scan-operations","content":"If start row, end row and limit ( say N ) are specified and N \\< number of rows between start row and end row, then N rows from start row will be returned to the user. If N > (number of rows between start row and end row (say M), then M number of rows will be returned to the user."},"4638":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-225","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"Endpoint"},"4639":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-226","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"HTTP Verb"},"4640":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-227","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"Description"},"4641":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-228","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"`/table/row_key`"},"4642":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-229","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"`PUT`"},"4643":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-230","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"Write a row to a table. The row, column qualifier, and value must each be Base-64 encoded. To encode a string, use the `base64` command-line utility. To decode the string, use `base64 -d`. The payload is in the `--data` argument, and the `/users/fakerow` value is a placeholder. Insert multiple rows by adding them to the `<CellSet>` element. You can also save the data to be inserted to a file and pass it to the `-d` parameter with syntax like `-d @filename.txt`."},"4644":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-231","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-put-operations","content":"**Example:**"},"4645":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-232","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Endpoint"},"4646":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-233","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"HTTP Verb"},"4647":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-234","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Description"},"4648":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-235","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`/table/row_key/?check=put`"},"4649":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-236","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`PUT`"},"4650":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-237","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Conditional Put - Change the current version value of a cell: Compare the current or latest version value (`current-version-value`) of a cell with the `check-value`, and if `current-version-value` == `check-value`, write new data (the `new-value`) into the cell as the current or latest version. The row, column qualifier, and value must each be Base-64 encoded. To encode a string, use the `base64` command-line utility. To decode the string, use `base64 -d`. The payload is in the `--data` or `-d` argument, with `the check cell name (column family:column name) and value` always at the end and right after `the new Put cell name (column family:column name) and value` of the same row key. You can also save the data to be inserted to a file and pass it to the `-d` parameter with syntax like `-d @filename.txt`."},"4651":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-238","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"**Example:**"},"4652":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-239","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Detailed Explanation:"},"4653":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-240","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"In the above json-format example:"},"4654":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-241","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`{\"column\":\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\", \"$\":\"TmV3R3V5\"}` at the end of `-d` option are `the check cell name and check cell value in Base-64` respectively: `\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\" for \"cfa:alias\"`, and `\"TmV3R3V5\" for \"NewGuy\"`"},"4655":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-242","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`{{\"column\":\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\",\"$\":\"T2xkR3V5\"}}` are `the new Put cell name and cell value in Base-64` respectively: `\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\" for \"cfa:alias\"`, and `\"T2xkR3V5\" for \"OldGuy\"`"},"4656":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-243","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`\"cm93MQ==\"` is `the Base-64 for \"row1\"` for the checkAndPut `row key`"},"4657":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-244","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"`\"/?check=put\"` after the `\"row key\" in the request URL` is required for checkAndPut WebHBase operation to work"},"4658":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-245","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"The `\"row key\" in the request URL` should be URL-encoded, e.g., `\"david%20chen\"` and `\"row1\"` are the URL-encoded formats of row keys `\"david chen\"` and `\"row1\"`, respectively"},"4659":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-246","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Note: \"cfa\" is the column family name and \"alias\" are the column (qualifier) name for the\nnon-Base64 encoded cell name."},"4660":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-247","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-put-operations","content":"Basically, the xml-format example is the same as the json-format example, and will not be explained here in detail."},"4661":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-248","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Endpoint"},"4662":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-249","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"HTTP Verb"},"4663":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-250","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Description"},"4664":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-251","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`/table/row_key/?check=delete`"},"4665":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-252","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`DELETE`"},"4666":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-253","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Conditional Deleting a Row: Compare the value of any version of a cell (`any-version-value`) with the `check-value`, and if `any-version-value` == `check-value`, delete the row specified by the `row_key` inside the requesting URL. The row, column qualifier, and value for checking in the payload must each be Base-64 encoded. To encode a string, use the base64 command-line utility. To decode the string, use base64 -d. The payload is in the --data argument. You can also save the data to be checked to a file and pass it to the `-d` parameter with syntax like `-d @filename.txt`."},"4667":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-254","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`/table/row_key/column_family/?check=delete`"},"4668":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-255","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`DELETE`"},"4669":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-256","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Conditional Deleting a Column Family of a Row: Compare the value of any version of a cell (`any-version-value`) with the `check-value`, and if `any-version-value` == `check-value`, delete the column family of a row specified by the `row_key/column_family` inside the requesting URL. Anything else is the same as those in `Conditional Deleting a Row`."},"4670":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-257","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`/table/row_key/column:qualifier/?check=delete`"},"4671":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-258","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`DELETE`"},"4672":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-259","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Conditional Deleting All Versions of a Column of a Row: Compare the value of any version of a cell (`any-version-value`) with the `check-value`, and if `any-version-value` == `check-value`, delete the column of a row specified by the `row_key/column:qualifier` inside the requesting URL. The `column:qualifier` in the requesting URL is the `column_family:column_name`. Anything else is the same as those in `Conditional Deleting a Row`."},"4673":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-260","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`/table/row_key/column:qualifier/version_id/?check=delete`"},"4674":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-261","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`DELETE`"},"4675":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-262","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Conditional Deleting a Single Version of a Column of a Row: Compare the value of any version of a cell (`any-version-value`) with the `check-value`, and if `any-version-value` == `check-value`, delete the version of a column of a row specified by the `row_key/column:qualifier/version_id` inside the requesting URL. The `column:qualifier` in the requesting URL is the `column_family:column_name`. The `version_id` in the requesting URL is a number, which equals to `the timestamp of the targeted version + 1`. Anything else is the same as those in `Conditional Deleting a Row`."},"4676":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-263","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"**Examples:**"},"4677":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-264","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"Detailed Explanation:"},"4678":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-265","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"In the above 4 json-format examples:"},"4679":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-266","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`{\"column\":\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\", \"$\":\"TmV3R3V5\"}` at the end of `-d` option are `the check cell name and check cell value in Base-64` respectively: `\"Y2ZhOmFsaWFz\" for \"cfa:alias\"`, and `\"TmV3R3V5\" for \"NewGuy\"`"},"4680":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-267","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`\"cm93MQ==\"` is `the Base-64 for \"row1\"` for the checkAndDelete `row key`"},"4681":{"id":"/docs/external-apis-268","page_id":"/docs/external-apis","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/external-apis#endpoints-for-check-and-delete-operations","content":"`\"/?check=delete\"` at the end of `the request URL` is required for checkAndDelete WebHBase operation to w