ge"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"Sink"},"6426":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-221","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"AgeOfLastAppliedOp"},"6427":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-222","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"How long it took to apply the last successful shipped edit."},"6428":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-223","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"Sink"},"6429":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-224","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"TimeStampsOfLastAppliedOp"},"6430":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-225","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"Date of last successful applied edit."},"6431":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-226","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#understanding-the-output","content":"Growing values for `Source.TimeStampsOfLastAppliedOp` and/or `Source.Replication Lag` would indicate replication delays. If those numbers keep going up, while `Source.TimeStampOfLastShippedOp`, `Source.EditsReadFromLogQueue`, `Source.OpsShippedToTarget` or `Source.TimeStampOfNextToReplicate` do not change at all, then replication flow is failing to progress, and there might be problems within clusters communication. This could also happen if replication is manually paused (via hbase shell `disable_peer` command, for example), but data keeps getting ingested in the source cluster tables."},"6432":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-227","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replication-observability-framework","content":"The core idea is to create `replication marker rows` periodically and insert them into WAL. These marker rows will help track the replication delays/bugs back to the `originating region server, WAL and timestamp of occurrence`. This tracker rows' WAL entries are interleaved with the regular table WAL entries and have a very high chance of running into the same replication delays/bugs that the user tables are seeing. Details as follows:"},"6433":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-228","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"Create a new table called `REPLICATION.WALEVENTTRACKER` table and persist all the WAL events (like `ACTIVE`, `ROLLING`, `ROLLED`) to this table.\\\nThe properties of this table are: Replication is set to 0, Block Cache is Disabled, Max versions is 1, TTL is 1 year."},"6434":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-229","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"This table has single ColumnFamily: `info`\\\n`info` contains multiple qualifiers:"},"6435":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-230","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"`info:region_server_name`"},"6436":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-231","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"`info:wal_name`"},"6437":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-232","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"`info:timestamp`"},"6438":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-233","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"`info:wal_state`"},"6439":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-234","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"`info:wal_length`"},"6440":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-235","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"Whenever we roll a WAL (`old-wal-name` → `new-wal-name`), it will create 3 rows in this table.\\\n`<region_server_name>, <old-wal-name>, <current timestamp>, <ROLLING>, <length of old-wal-name>`\\\n`<region_server_name>, <old-wal-name>, <current timestamp>, <ROLLED>, <length of old-wal-name>`\\\n`<region_server_name>, <new-wal-name>, <current timestamp>, <ACTIVE>, 0`"},"6441":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-236","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationwaleventtracker-table","content":"**Configuration**\\\nTo enable persisting WAL events, there is a configuration property: `hbase.regionserver.wal.event.tracker.enabled` (defaults to false)"},"6442":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-237","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"Create a new table called `REPLICATION.SINK_TRACKER`.\\\nThe properties of this table are: Replication is set to 0, Block Cache is Disabled, Max versions is 1, TTL is 1 year."},"6443":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-238","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"This table has single ColumnFamily: `info`\\\n`info` contains multiple qualifiers:"},"6444":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-239","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"`info:region_server_name`"},"6445":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-240","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"`info:wal_name`"},"6446":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-241","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"`info:timestamp`"},"6447":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-242","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"`info:offset`"},"6448":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-243","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationsink_tracker-table","content":"**Configuration**\\\nTo create the above table, there is a configuration property: `hbase.regionserver.replication.sink.tracker.enabled` (defaults to false)"},"6449":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-244","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationmarker-chore","content":"We introduced a new chore called `ReplicationMarkerChore` which will create the marker rows periodically into active WAL. The marker rows has the following metadata: `region_server_name, wal_name, timestamp and offset within WAL`. These markers are replicated (with special handling) and they are persisted into a sink side table `REPLICATION.SINK_TRACKER`."},"6450":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-245","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#replicationmarker-chore","content":"**Configuration:**\\\n`ReplicationMarkerChore` is enabled with configuration property: `hbase.regionserver.replication.marker.enabled` (defaults to false) and the period at which it creates marker rows is controlled by `hbase.regionserver.replication.marker.chore.duration` (defaults to 30 seconds). Sink cluster can choose to process these marker rows and persist to `REPLICATION.SINK_TRACKER` table or it can ignore these rows. This behavior is controlled by configuration property `hbase.regionserver.replication.sink.tracker.enabled` (defaults to false). If set to false, it will ignore the marker rows."},"6451":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-246","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#how-to-enable-end-to-end-feature-","content":"To use this whole feature, we will need to enable the above configuration properties in 2 phases/releases.\\\nIn first phase/release, set the following configuration properties to `true`:"},"6452":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-247","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#how-to-enable-end-to-end-feature-","content":"`hbase.regionserver.wal.event.tracker.enabled`: This will just persist all the WAL events to REPLICATION.WALEVENTTRACKER table."},"6453":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-248","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#how-to-enable-end-to-end-feature-","content":"`hbase.regionserver.replication.sink.tracker.enabled`: This will create REPLICATION.SINK\\_TRACKER table and will process special marker rows coming from source cluster."},"6454":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-249","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#how-to-enable-end-to-end-feature-","content":"In second phase/release, set the following configuration property to `true`:"},"6455":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication-250","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/cluster-replication#how-to-enable-end-to-end-feature-","content":"`hbase.regionserver.replication.marker.enabled`: This will create marker rows periodically and sink cluster will persist these marker rows in `REPLICATION.SINK_TRACKER` table."},"6456":{"id":"/docs/operational-management","page_id":"/docs/operational-management","type":"page","content":"Apache HBase Operational Management","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Operations & Development","Apache HBase Operational Management"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/operational-management"},"6457":{"id":"/docs/operational-management-0","page_id":"/docs/operational-management","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management","content":"This chapter will cover operational tools and practices required of a running Apache HBase cluster."},"6458":{"id":"/docs/operational-management-1","page_id":"/docs/operational-management","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management","content":"The subject of operations is related to the topics of Troubleshooting and Debugging Apache HBase, Apache HBase Performance Tuning, and Apache HBase Configuration but is a distinct topic in itself."},"6459":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring","type":"page","content":"Metrics & Monitoring","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Multi-Page Documentation","Operations & Development","Apache HBase Operational Management"],"tags":["multi-page"],"url":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring"},"6460":{"id":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring-0","page_id":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring","tags":["multi-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/operational-management/metrics-and-monitoring","conte