e-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#filters","content":"Less than"},"18048":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8248","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#filters","content":"\\<="},"18049":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8249","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#filters","content":"Less than and equal to"},"18050":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8250","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#filters","content":"You can see the current filters by pressing `^o` key and clear them by pressing `=` key."},"18051":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8251","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#drilling-down","content":"You can drill down the metric record by choosing a metric record that you want to drill down and pressing `i` key in the top screen. With this feature, you can find hot regions easily in a top-down manner."},"18052":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8252","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#help-screen","content":"You can see the help screen by pressing `h` key in the top screen."},"18053":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8253","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#how-hbtop-gets-the-metrics-data","content":"hbtop gets the metrics from ClusterMetrics which is returned as the result of a call to Admin#getClusterMetrics() on the current HMaster. To add metrics to hbtop, they will need to be exposed via ClusterMetrics."},"18054":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8254","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#tracing-overview","content":"The basic support for tracing has been done, where we added tracing for async client, rpc, region read/write/scan operation, and WAL. We use opentelemetry-api to implement the tracing support manually by code, as our code base is way too complicated to be instrumented through a java agent. But notice that you still need to attach the opentelemetry java agent to enable tracing. Please see the official site for OpenTelemetry and the documentation for opentelemetry-java-instrumentation for more details on how to properly configure opentelemetry instrumentation."},"18055":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8255","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#enable-tracing","content":"See this section in hbase-env.sh"},"18056":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8256","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#enable-tracing","content":"Uncomment this line to enable tracing. The default config is to output the tracing data to log. Please see the documentation for opentelemetry-java-instrumentation for more details on how to export tracing data to other tracing system such as OTel collector, jaeger or zipkin, what does the *service.name* mean, and how to change the sampling rate, etc."},"18057":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8257","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#enable-tracing","content":"The\nLoggingSpanExporter\nuses java.util.logging(jul) for logging tracing data, and the logger is initialized in\nopentelemetry java agent, which seems to be ahead of our jul to slf4j bridge initialization, so it\nwill always log the tracing data to console. We highly suggest that you use other tracing systems\nto collect and view tracing data instead of logging."},"18058":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8258","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#performance-impact","content":"According to the result in HBASE-25658, the performance impact is minimal. Of course the test cluster is not under heavy load, so if you find out that enabling tracing would impact the performance, try to lower the sampling rate. See documentation for configuring sampler for more details."},"18059":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8259","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-overview","content":"Historically, HBase internals have relied on creating hfiles on temporary directories first, renaming\nthose files to the actual store directory at operation commit time. That's a simple and convenient\nway to separate transient from already finalised files that are ready to serve client reads with data.\nThis approach works well with strong consistent file systems, but with the popularity of less consistent\nfile systems, mainly Object Store which can be used like file systems, dependency on atomic rename operations starts to introduce performance penalties. The Amazon S3 Object Store, in particular, has been the most affected deployment,\ndue to its lack of atomic renames. The HBase community temporarily bypassed this problem by building a distributed locking layer called HBOSS, to guarantee atomicity of operations against S3."},"18060":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8260","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-overview","content":"With **Store File Tracking**, decision on where to originally create new hfiles and how to proceed upon\ncommit is delegated to the specific Store File Tracking implementation.\nThe implementation can be set at the HBase service leve in **hbase-site.xml** or at the\nTable or Column Family via the TableDescriptor configuration."},"18061":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8261","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-overview","content":"When the store file tracking implementation is specified in **hbase\\_site.xml**, this configuration\nis also propagated into a tables configuration at table creation time. This is to avoid dangerous\nconfiguration mismatches between processes, which could potentially lead to data loss."},"18062":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8262","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#available-implementations","content":"Store File Tracking initial version provides three builtin implementations:"},"18063":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8263","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#available-implementations","content":"DEFAULT"},"18064":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8264","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#available-implementations","content":"FILE"},"18065":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8265","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#available-implementations","content":"MIGRATION"},"18066":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8266","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-default","content":"As per the name, this is the Store File Tracking implementation used by default when no explicit\nconfiguration has been defined. The DEFAULT tracker implements the standard approach using temporary\ndirectories and renames. This is how all previous (implicit) implementation that HBase used to track store files."},"18067":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8267","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#file","content":"A file tracker implementation that creates new files straight in the store directory, avoiding the\nneed for rename operations. It keeps a list of committed hfiles in memory, backed by meta files, in\neach store directory. Whenever a new hfile is committed, the list of *tracked files* in the given\nstore is updated and a new meta file is written with this list contents, discarding the previous\nmeta file now containing an out dated list."},"18068":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8268","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#migration","content":"A special implementation to be used when swapping between Store File Tracking implementations on\npre-existing tables that already contain data, and therefore, files being tracked under an specific\nlogic."},"18069":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8269","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-usage","content":"For fresh deployments that don't yet contain any user data, **FILE** implementation can be just set as\nvalue for **hbase.store.file-tracker.impl** property in global **hbase-site.xml** configuration, prior\nto the first hbase start. Omitting this property sets the **DEFAULT** implementation."},"18070":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8270","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-usage","content":"For clusters with data that are upgraded to a version of HBase containing the store file tracking\nfeature, the Store File Tracking implementation can only be changed with the **MIGRATION**\nimplementation, so that the *new tracker* can safely build its list of tracked files based on the\nlist of the *current tracker*."},"18071":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8271","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#store-file-tracking-usage","content":"MIGRATION tracker should NOT be set at global configuration. To use it, follow below section about\nsetting Store File Tacking at Table or Column Family configuration."},"18072":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8272","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#configuring-for-table-or-column-family","content":"Setting Store File Tracking configuration globally may not always be possible or desired, for example,\nin the case of upgraded clusters with pre-existing user data.\nStore File Tracking can be set at Table or Column Family level configuration.\nFor example, to specify **FILE** implementation in the table configuration at table creation time,\nthe following should be applied:"},"18073":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8273","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#configuring-for-table-or-column-family","content":"To define **FILE** for an specific Column Family:"},"18074":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8274","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#switching-trackers-at-table-or-column-family","content":"A very common scenario is to set Store File Tracking on pre-existing HBase deployments that have\nbeen upgraded to a version that supports this feature. To apply the FILE tracker, tables effectively\nneed to be migrated from the DEFAULT tracker to the FILE tracker. As explained previously, such\nprocess requires the usage of the special MIGRATION tracker implementation, which can only be\nspecified at table or Column Family level."},"18075":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8275","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#switching-trackers-at-table-or-column-family","content":"For example, to switch *tracker* from **DEFAULT** to **FILE** in a table configuration:"},"18076":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8276","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#switching-trackers-at-table-or-column-family","content":"To apply similar switch at column family level configuration:"},"18077":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8277","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#switching-trackers-at-table-or-column-family","content":"Once all table regions have been onlined again, don't forget to disable MIGRATION, by now setting\n**hbase.store.file-tracker.migration.dst.impl** value as the **hbase.store.file-tracker.impl**. In the above\nexample, that would be as follows:"},"18078":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8278","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#specifying-trackers-during-snapshot-recovery","content":"It's also possible to specify a given store file tracking implementation when recovering a snapshot\nusing the *CLONE\\_SFT* option of *clone\\_snasphot* command. This is useful when recovering old\nsnapshots, taken prior to a change in the global configuration, or if the snapshot has been\nimported from a different cluster that had a different store file tracking setting.\nBecause snapshots preserve table and colum family descriptors, a simple restore would reload\nthe original configuration, requiring the additional steps described above to convert the\ntable/column family to the desired tracker implementation.\nAn example of how to use *clone\\_snapshot* to specify the **FILE** tracker implementation\nis shown below:"},"18079":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8279","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#specifying-trackers-during-snapshot-recovery","content":"The option to specify the tracker during snapshot recovery is only available for the\n*clone\\_snapshot* command. The *restore\\_snapshot* command does not support this parameter."},"18080":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8280","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#bulk-data-generator-tool-usage","content":"Examples:"},"18081":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8281","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#table-schema","content":"Tool generates a HBase table with single column family, i.e. **cf** and 9 columns i.e."},"18082":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8282","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#table-schema","content":"with row key as"},"18083":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8283","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#table-creation","content":"Tool creates a pre-splited HBase Table having \"**split-count**\" splits (i.e. **split-count** + 1 regions) with sequential 6 digit region boundary prefix.\nExample: If a table is generated with \"**split-count**\" as 10, it will have (10+1) regions with following start-end keys."},"18084":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8284","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Tool creates and run a MR job to generate the HFiles, which are bulk loaded to table regions via `org.apache.hadoop.hbase.tool.BulkLoadHFilesTool`.\nThe number of mappers is defined in input as \"**mapper-count**\". Each mapper generates \"**records-per-mapper**\" rows."},"18085":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8285","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"`org.apache.hadoop.hbase.util.bulkdatageneratorBulkDataGeneratorRecordReader` ensures that each record generated by mapper is associated with index (added to the key) ranging from 1 to \"**records-per-mapper**\"."},"18086":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8286","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"The TOOL\\_EVENT\\_ID column for each row has a 6 digit prefix as"},"18087":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8287","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Example, if 10 records are to be generated by each mapper and \"**split-count**\" is 4, the TOOL\\_EVENT\\_IDs for each record will have a prefix as"},"18088":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8288","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Record Index"},"18089":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8289","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"TOOL\\_EVENT\\_ID's first six characters"},"18090":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8290","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"1"},"18091":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8291","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000001"},"18092":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8292","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"2"},"18093":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8293","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000002"},"18094":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8294","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"3"},"18095":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8295","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000003"},"18096":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8296","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"4"},"18097":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8297","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000004"},"18098":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8298","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"5"},"18099":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8299","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000000"},"18100":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8300","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"6"},"18101":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8301","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000001"},"18102":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8302","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"7"},"18103":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8303","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000002"},"18104":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8304","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"8"},"18105":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8305","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000003"},"18106":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8306","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"9"},"18107":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8307","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000004"},"18108":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8308","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"10"},"18109":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8309","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"000005"},"18110":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8310","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Since TOOL\\_EVENT\\_ID is first attribute of row key and table region boundaries are also having start-end keys as 6 digit sequential prefixes, this ensures that each mapper generates (nearly) same number of rows for each region, making the data uniformly distributed.\nTOOL\\_EVENT\\_ID suffix and other columns of the row are populated with random data."},"18111":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8311","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Number of rows generated is"},"18112":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8312","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#data-generation","content":"Size of each rows is (approximately)"},"18113":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8313","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"These results are from a 11 node cluster having HBase and Hadoop service running within self-managed test environment"},"18114":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8314","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"Data Size"},"18115":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8315","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"Time to Generate Data (mins)"},"18116":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8316","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"100 GB"},"18117":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8317","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"6 minutes"},"18118":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8318","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"340 GB"},"18119":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8319","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"13 minutes"},"18120":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8320","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"3.5 TB"},"18121":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8321","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#experiments","content":"3 hours 10 minutes"},"18122":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8322","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"The Apache HBase project welcomes contributions to all aspects of the project, including the documentation."},"18123":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8323","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"In HBase, documentation includes the following areas, and probably some others:"},"18124":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8324","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"The HBase Reference Guide (this book)"},"18125":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8325","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"The HBase website"},"18126":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8326","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"API documentation"},"18127":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8327","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"Command-line utility output and help text"},"18128":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8328","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"Web UI strings, explicit help text, context-sensitive strings, and others"},"18129":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8329","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"Log messages"},"18130":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8330","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"Comments in source files, configuration files, and others"},"18131":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8331","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"Localization of any of the above into target languages other than English"},"18132":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8332","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#appendix-contributing-to-documentation","content":"No matter which area you want to help out with, the first step is almost always to download (typically by cloning the Git repository) and familiarize yourself with the HBase source code. For information on downloading and building the source, see developer."},"18133":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8333","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#contributing-to-other-strings","content":"If you spot an error in a string in a UI, utility, script, log message, or elsewhere, or you think something could be made more clear, or you think text needs to be added where it doesn't currently exist, the first step is to file a JIRA. Be sure to set the component to `Documentation` in addition to any other involved components. Most components have one or more default owners, who monitor new issues which come into those queues. Regardless of whether you feel able to fix the bug, you should still file bugs where you see them."},"18134":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8334","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#contributing-to-other-strings","content":"If you want to try your hand at fixing your newly-filed bug, assign it to yourself. You will need to clone the HBase Git repository to your local system and work on the issue there. When you have developed a potential fix, submit it for review. If it addresses the issue and is seen as an improvement, one of the HBase committers will commit it to one or more branches, as appropriate."},"18135":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8335","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"This procedure goes into more detail than Git pros will need, but is included in this appendix so that people unfamiliar with Git can feel confident contributing to HBase while they learn."},"18136":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8336","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"If you have not already done so, clone the Git repository locally. You only need to do this once."},"18137":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8337","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"Fairly often, pull remote changes into your local repository by using the `git pull` command,\nwhile your tracking branch is checked out."},"18138":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8338","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"For each issue you work on, create a new branch. One convention that works well for naming the branches is to name a given branch the same as the JIRA it relates to:"},"18139":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8339","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"Make your suggested changes on your branch, committing your changes to your local repository\noften. If you need to switch to working on a different issue, remember to check out the\nappropriate branch."},"18140":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8340","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"When you are ready to submit your patch, first be sure that HBase builds cleanly and behaves as\nexpected in your modified branch."},"18141":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8341","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"If you have made documentation or website changes, verify that the site builds correctly by\nrunning the development server from the `hbase-website/` directory."},"18142":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8342","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"If it takes you several days or weeks to implement your fix, or you know that the area of the code you are working in has had a lot of changes lately, make sure you rebase your branch against the remote master and take care of any conflicts before submitting your patch."},"18143":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8343","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"Generate your patch against the remote master. Run the following command from the top level of your git repository (usually called `hbase`):"},"18144":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8344","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"The name of the patch should contain the JIRA ID."},"18145":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8345","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"Look over the patch file to be sure that you did not change any additional files by accident and\nthat there are no other surprises."},"18146":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8346","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"When you are satisfied, attach the patch to the JIRA and click the **Patch Available** button. A\nreviewer will review your patch."},"18147":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8347","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#procedure-suggested-work-flow-for-submitting-patches","content":"If you need to submit a new version of the patch, leave the old one on the JIRA and add a version\nnumber to the name of the new patch."},"18148":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8348","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"The HBase website and documentation are now part of a single application built with Remix and Fumadocs. The source files are located in the `hbase-website/` directory:"},"18149":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8349","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"**Documentation pages**: `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/(multi-page)/` - individual MDX files for each documentation section"},"18150":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8350","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"**Single-page view**: `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/single-page/index.mdx` - combines all documentation into one page"},"18151":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8351","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"**Website components**: `hbase-website/app/components/` - React components used throughout the site"},"18152":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8352","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"**Images**: `hbase-website/public/` - static assets including images"},"18153":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8353","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#editing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"You can edit MDX files in any text editor or IDE. To preview your changes locally, run the development server from the `hbase-website/` directory and navigate to the documentation pages in your browser. When you are satisfied with your changes, follow the procedure in submit doc patch procedure to submit your patch."},"18154":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8354","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#publishing-the-hbase-website-and-documentation","content":"The HBase website and documentation are built and deployed as a single Remix application. The deployment process is managed through the project's CI/CD pipeline, which builds the site from the `hbase-website/` directory and deploys it automatically when changes are merged to the main branch."},"18155":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8355","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#mdx-and-fumadocs-components","content":"The HBase documentation is written in MDX (Markdown with JSX), which allows you to use standard Markdown syntax along with React components. For comprehensive documentation on Markdown formatting and MDX features, refer to:"},"18156":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8356","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#mdx-and-fumadocs-components","content":"Fumadocs Markdown Documentation - Complete guide to MDX syntax and Fumadocs features"},"18157":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8357","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#mdx-and-fumadocs-components","content":"CommonMark specification - Standard Markdown syntax reference"},"18158":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8358","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#mdx-and-fumadocs-components","content":"GFM (GitHub Flavored Markdown) - GitHub-style Markdown extensions"},"18159":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8359","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#fumadocs-components","content":"Fumadocs provides several components that enhance the documentation:"},"18160":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8360","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#steps-component","content":"Use `<Steps>` to create numbered step-by-step instructions:"},"18161":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8361","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#steps-component","content":"**Example output:**"},"18162":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8362","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#callout-component","content":"Use `<Callout>` for notes, warnings, and important information:"},"18163":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8363","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#callout-component","content":"**Example output:**"},"18164":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8364","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#include-directive","content":"The single-page documentation view uses `<include>` tags to combine multiple MDX files:"},"18165":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8365","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#include-directive","content":"See `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/single-page/index.mdx` for examples of how all documentation sections are included in the single-page view."},"18166":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8366","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#auto-generated-content","content":"Some parts of the HBase documentation, such as the default configuration, are generated automatically to stay in sync with the code. The configuration documentation is generated from the `hbase-common/src/main/resources/hbase-default.xml` file."},"18167":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8367","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#auto-generated-content","content":"To add or modify configuration parameters, update the source XML file. To regenerate the documentation from the updated configuration, run:"},"18168":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8368","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#auto-generated-content","content":"This command is also executed automatically when you run `npm ci`."},"18169":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8369","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#images-in-the-documentation","content":"You can include images in the HBase documentation using standard Markdown syntax. Always include descriptive alt text for accessibility:"},"18170":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8370","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#images-in-the-documentation","content":"Save images to the `hbase-website/public/` directory or an appropriate subdirectory. Reference them in your MDX files using absolute paths from the public directory:"},"18171":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8371","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#images-in-the-documentation","content":"When submitting a patch that includes images, attach the images to the JIRA issue."},"18172":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8372","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"To add a new section to the HBase documentation:"},"18173":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8373","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"Create a new MDX file in `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/(multi-page)/` with a descriptive name (e.g., `my-new-section.mdx`)"},"18174":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8374","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"Add frontmatter at the top of the file with a title and description:"},"18175":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8375","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"Add your new file to `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/(multi-page)/meta.json` in the appropriate location within the `pages` array (without the `.mdx` extension):"},"18176":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8376","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"Add an `<include>` directive to `hbase-website/app/pages/_docs/docs/_mdx/single-page/index.mdx` in the appropriate location:"},"18177":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8377","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#adding-a-new-section-to-the-documentation","content":"Add your new file to Git before creating your patch."},"18178":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8378","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#unique-headings-requirement","content":"Since all documentation files are merged into a single-page view, **all heading IDs must be unique across the entire documentation**. A test will fail during the build if duplicate heading IDs are detected, marking the problematic headings."},"18179":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8379","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#unique-headings-requirement","content":"Headings don't have to be visually unique, but their link IDs must be unique. You can customize the heading ID using Fumadocs syntax:"},"18180":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8380","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#unique-headings-requirement","content":"This creates a heading that displays as \"Configuration\" but has the unique ID `#server-configuration` for linking purposes."},"18181":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8381","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#hiding-headings-from-table-of-contents","content":"You can hide specific headings from the right-side table of contents:"},"18182":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8382","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#hiding-headings-from-table-of-contents","content":"This heading will still appear in the document but won't show up in the table of contents navigation."},"18183":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8383","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#hiding-headings-from-table-of-contents","content":"Note: `[!toc]` becomes part of the heading ID. For example, `## Usage [!toc]` will have the ID\n`#usage-toc`."},"18184":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8384","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#combining-custom-ids-and-toc-hiding","content":"You can combine both attributes:"},"18185":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8385","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"The following documentation issues come up often:"},"18186":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8386","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"**Isolate Changes for Easy Diff Review**"},"18187":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8387","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"Avoid reformatting entire files when making content changes. If you need to reformat a file, do that in a separate JIRA where you do not change any content."},"18188":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8388","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"**Syntax Highlighting**"},"18189":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8389","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"MDX supports syntax highlighting for code blocks. Specify the language after the opening triple backticks:"},"18190":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8390","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"**Component Syntax**"},"18191":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8391","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"Remember to properly close Fumadocs components. Components like `<Steps>` and `<Callout>` must be properly closed:"},"18192":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8392","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"**Unique Heading IDs**"},"18193":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8393","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#common-documentation-issues","content":"Ensure all heading IDs are unique across the entire documentation. If you get a test failure about duplicate headings, customize the heading ID using `[#custom-id]` syntax as described in the Unique Headings Requirement section."},"18194":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8394","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#faq-when-should-i-use-hbase","content":"See Overview in the Architecture chapter."},"18195":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8395","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#does-hbase-support-sql","content":"Not really. SQL-ish support for HBase via Hive is in development, however Hive is based on MapReduce which is not generally suitable for low-latency requests. See the Data Model section for examples on the HBase client."},"18196":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8396","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#how-can-i-find-examples-of-nosqlhbase","content":"See the link to the BigTable paper in Other Information About HBase, as well as the other papers."},"18197":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8397","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#what-is-the-history-of-hbase","content":"See HBase History."},"18198":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8398","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#why-are-the-cells-above-10mb-not-recommended-for-hbase","content":"Large cells don't fit well into HBase's approach to buffering data. First, the large cells bypass the MemStoreLAB when they are written. Then, they cannot be cached in the L2 block cache during read operations. Instead, HBase has to allocate on-heap memory for them each time. This can have a significant impact on the garbage collector within the RegionServer process."},"18199":{"id":"/docs/single-page-8399","page_id":"/docs/single-page","tags":["single-page"],"type":"text","url":"/docs/single-page#how-do-i-upgrade-maven-managed-projects-from-hbase-094-to-hbase-096","content":"In HBase 0.96, the project moved to a modular structure. Adjust your project's dependencies to rely upon the `hbase-client` module or another module as appropriate, rather than a single JAR. You can model your Maven dependency after one of the following, depending on your targeted version of HBase. See Section 3.5, \"Upgrading from 0.94.x to 0.96.x\" or Section 3.3, \"Upgrading from 0.96.x to 0.98.x\" for more information."},"18200":{"id":"/docs/sing