idth, and the valueids are fixed width)."],[13459,"(But the usernames are fixed width, and the valueids are fixed width)."],[9511,"(Eventually) Upgrade Clients"],[13027,"(Eventually) Upgrade Clients"],[7591,"(From Matteo's ProcedureV2 and Notification Bus doc)\\\nIn the case of asynchronous operations, the result must be kept around until the client asks for it. Once we receive a \"get\" of the result we can schedule the delete of the record. For some operations the result may be \"unnecessary\" especially in case of failure (e.g. if the create table fail, we can query the operation result or we can just do a list table to see if it was created) so in some cases we can schedule the delete after a timeout. On the client side the operation will return a \"Procedure ID\", this ID can be used to wait until the procedure is completed and get the result/exception."],[17554,"(From Matteo's ProcedureV2 and Notification Bus doc)\\\nIn the case of asynchronous operations, the result must be kept around until the client asks for it. Once we receive a \"get\" of the result we can schedule the delete of the record. For some operations the result may be \"unnecessary\" especially in case of failure (e.g. if the create table fail, we can query the operation result or we can just do a list table to see if it was created) so in some cases we can schedule the delete after a timeout. On the client side the operation will return a \"Procedure ID\", this ID can be used to wait until the procedure is completed and get the result/exception."],[7438,"(From Yu Li up in HBASE-17083)"],[15803,"(From Yu Li up in HBASE-17083)"],[1983,"(NOTE: Our IRC channel seems to have been deprecated in favor of the above Slack channel)"],[16995,"(NOTE: Our IRC channel seems to have been deprecated in favor of the above Slack channel)"],[7822,"(note: the lead byte is listed to the right as a comment.) Given that the first split is a '0' and the last split is an 'f', everything is great, right? Not so fast."]