me to verify user specified credentials against a configured LDAP (or Active Directory) server. The authentication filter must be configured with the following init parameters:"],[8881,"**InclusiveStopFilter**\\\nThis filter takes one argument – a row key on which to stop scanning.\nIt returns all key-values present in rows up to and including the specified row."],[15416,"**InclusiveStopFilter**\\\nThis filter takes one argument – a row key on which to stop scanning.\nIt returns all key-values present in rows up to and including the specified row."],[5012,"**interface MasterObserver**"],[18966,"**interface MasterObserver**"],[5120,"**interface PriorityFunction**"],[19074,"**interface PriorityFunction**"],[5044,"**interface RegionObserver**"],[18998,"**interface RegionObserver**"],[5291,"**interface Table**"],[19245,"**interface Table**"],[5074,"**interface WALObserver**"],[19028,"**interface WALObserver**"],[4050,"**Isolate Changes for Easy Diff Review**"],[18186,"**Isolate Changes for Easy Diff Review**"],[8381,"**Java API example:**"],[13885,"**Java API example:**"],[8370,"**Java API:**"],[8373,"**Java API:**"],[8376,"**Java API:**"],[13874,"**Java API:**"],[13877,"**Java API:**"],[13880,"**Java API:**"],[4710,"**JDO Example**\\\nThis example uses JDO to create a table and an index, insert a row into a table, get a row, get a column value, perform a query, and do some additional HBase operations."],[15343,"**JDO Example**\\\nThis example uses JDO to create a table and an index, insert a row into a table, get a row, get a column value, perform a query, and do some additional HBase operations."],[326,"**Key:**"],[13959,"**Key:**"],[8873,"**KeyOnlyFilter**\\\nThis filter doesn't take any arguments.\nIt returns only the key component of each key-value."],[15408,"**KeyOnlyFilter**\\\nThis filter doesn't take any arguments.\nIt returns only the key component of each key-value."],[1161,"**Keys**\\\nThe values that are stored are only half the picture, since each value is