ating all steps, rather than a portion, building a RC."],[1995,"*Discuss in public*: Use the mailing lists to discuss what you've discovered\nand see if there is something you've missed. Avoid using back channels, so\nthat you benefit from the experience and expertise of the project as a whole."],[17007,"*Discuss in public*: Use the mailing lists to discuss what you've discovered\nand see if there is something you've missed. Avoid using back channels, so\nthat you benefit from the experience and expertise of the project as a whole."],[1996,"*Don't file on behalf of others*: You might not have all the context, and you\ndon't have as much motivation to see it through as the person who is actually\nexperiencing the bug. It's more helpful in the long term to encourage others\nto file their own issues. Point them to this material and offer to help out\nthe first time or two."],[17008,"*Don't file on behalf of others*: You might not have all the context, and you\ndon't have as much motivation to see it through as the person who is actually\nexperiencing the bug. It's more helpful in the long term to encourage others\nto file their own issues. Point them to this material and offer to help out\nthe first time or two."],[5978,"*EAGER*: This is *BASIC* policy plus in-memory compaction of flushes (much like the on-disk compactions done to hfiles); on compaction we apply on-disk rules eliminating versions, duplicates, ttl'd cells, etc."],[14845,"*EAGER*: This is *BASIC* policy plus in-memory compaction of flushes (much like the on-disk compactions done to hfiles); on compaction we apply on-disk rules eliminating versions, duplicates, ttl'd cells, etc."],[4829,"*Example extract from *hbase-env.sh* where *JAVA\\_HOME* is set*"],[11789,"*Example extract from *hbase-env.sh* where *JAVA\\_HOME* is set*"],[8274,"*Execute (X)* - can execute coprocessor endpoints at the given scope"],[13778,"*Execute (X)* - can execute coprocessor endpoints at the given scope"],[7561,"*execute()* retur