 Effectively, the value of `hbase.hstore.compaction.max` controls the length of time it takes a single compaction to complete. Setting it larger means that more StoreFiles are included in a compaction. For most cases, the default value is appropriate.\\\n**Default**: 10"],[14500,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max`\nThe maximum number of StoreFiles which will be selected for a single minor compaction, regardless of the number of eligible StoreFiles. Effectively, the value of `hbase.hstore.compaction.max` controls the length of time it takes a single compaction to complete. Setting it larger means that more StoreFiles are included in a compaction. For most cases, the default value is appropriate.\\\n**Default**: 10"],[956,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` (files) Maximum number of StoreFiles to compact per minor compaction (default 10)."],[14519,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` (files) Maximum number of StoreFiles to compact per minor compaction (default 10)."],[3326,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` [!toc]"],[9993,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` [!toc]"],[963,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[976,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[988,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[14526,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[14539,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[14551,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.max` = 5 (files)"],[957,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` (bytes) Any StoreFile smaller than this setting with automatically be a candidate for compaction. Defaults to `hbase.hregion.memstore.flush.size` (128 mb)."],[14520,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` (bytes) Any StoreFile smaller than this setting with automatically be a candidate for compaction. Defaults to `hbase.hregion.memstore.flush.size` (128 mb)."],[3327,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` [!toc]"],[9994,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` [!toc]"],[964,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[977,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[989,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[14527,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[14540,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[14552,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` = 10 (bytes)"],[938,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size`\\\nA StoreFile smaller than this size will always be eligible for minor compaction. StoreFiles this size or larger are evaluated by `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` to determine if they are eligible. Because this limit represents the \"automatic include\" limit for all StoreFiles smaller than this value, this value may need to be reduced in write-heavy environments where many files in the 1-2 MB range are being flushed, because every StoreFile will be targeted for compaction and the resulting StoreFiles may still be under the minimum size and require further compaction. If this parameter is lowered, the ratio check is triggered more quickly. This addressed some issues seen in earlier versions of HBase but changing this parameter is no longer necessary in most situations.\\\n**Default**:128 MB"],[14501,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size`\\\nA StoreFile smaller than this size will always be eligible for minor compaction. StoreFiles this size or larger are evaluated by `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` to determine if they are eligible. Because this limit represents the \"automatic include\" limit for all StoreFiles smaller than this value, this value may need to be reduced in write-heavy environments where many files in the 1-2 MB range are being flushed, because every StoreFile will be targeted for compaction and the resulting StoreFiles may still be under the minimum size and require further compaction. If this parameter is lowered, the ratio check is triggered more quickly. This addressed some issues seen in earlier versions of HBase but changing this parameter is no longer necessary in most situations.\\\n**Default**:128 MB"],[955,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` (in HBase v 0.90 this is called `hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold`) (files) Minimum number of StoreFiles per Store to be selected for a compaction to occur (default 2)."],[14518,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` (in HBase v 0.90 this is called `hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold`) (files) Minimum number of StoreFiles per Store to be selected for a compaction to occur (default 2)."],[3325,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` [!toc]"],[9992,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` [!toc]"],[962,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[975,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[987,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[14525,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[14538,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[14550,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min` = 3 (files)"],[936,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min`\\\nThe minimum number of StoreFiles which must be eligible for compaction before compaction can run. The goal of tuning `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` is to avoid ending up with too many tiny StoreFiles to compact. Setting this value to 2 would cause a minor compaction each time you have two StoreFiles in a Store, and this is probably not appropriate. If you set this value too high, all the other values will need to be adjusted accordingly. For most cases, the default value is appropriate. In previous versions of HBase, the parameter `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` was called `hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold`.\\\n**Default**: 3"],[14499,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.min`\\\nThe minimum number of StoreFiles which must be eligible for compaction before compaction can run. The goal of tuning `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` is to avoid ending up with too many tiny StoreFiles to compact. Setting this value to 2 would cause a minor compaction each time you have two StoreFiles in a Store, and this is probably not appropriate. If you set this value too high, all the other values will need to be adjusted accordingly. For most cases, the default value is appropriate. In previous versions of HBase, the parameter `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` was called `hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold`.\\\n**Default**: 3"],[3330,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio.offpeak` [!toc]"],[9997,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio.offpeak` [!toc]"],[944,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio.offpeak`\\\nThe compaction ratio used during off-peak compactions, if off-peak hours are also configured (see below). Expressed as a floating-point decimal. This allows for more aggressive (or less aggressive, if you set it lower than `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`) compaction during a set time period. Ignored if off-peak is disabled (default). This works the same as `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`.\\\n**Default**: `5.0F`"],[14507,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio.offpeak`\\\nThe compaction ratio used during off-peak compactions, if off-peak hours are also configured (see below). Expressed as a floating-point decimal. This allows for more aggressive (or less aggressive, if you set it lower than `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`) compaction during a set time period. Ignored if off-peak is disabled (default). This works the same as `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`.\\\n**Default**: `5.0F`"],[3329,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` [!toc]"],[9996,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` [!toc]"],[961,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[974,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[986,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[14524,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[14537,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[14549,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` = 1.0f"],[954,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` Ratio used in compaction file selection algorithm (default 1.2f)."],[14517,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` Ratio used in compaction file selection algorithm (default 1.2f)."],[940,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`\\\nFor minor compaction, this ratio is used to determine whether a given StoreFile which is larger than `hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` is eligible for compaction. Its effect is to limit compaction of large StoreFile. The value of `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` is expressed as a floating-point decimal."],[14503,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio`\\\nFor minor compaction, this ratio is used to determine whether a given StoreFile which is larger than `hbase.hstore.compaction.min.size` is eligible for compaction. Its effect is to limit compaction of large StoreFile. The value of `hbase.hstore.compaction.ratio` is expressed as a floating-point decimal."],[3347,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.throughput.higher.bound` [!toc]"],[10014,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.throughput.higher.bound` [!toc]"],[3346,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.throughput.lower.bound` [!toc]"],[10013,"`hbase.hstore.compaction.throughput.lower.bound` [!toc]"],[3320,"`hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold` [!toc]"],[9987,"`hbase.hstore.compactionThreshold` [!toc]"],[3322,"`hbase.hstore.flusher.count` [!toc]"],[9989,"`hbase.hstore.flusher.count` [!toc]"],[3331,"`hbase.hstore.time.to.purge.deletes` [!toc]"],[9998,"`hbase.hstore.time.to.purge.deletes` [!toc]"],[3432,"`hbase.http.filter.initializers` [!toc]"],[10099,"`hbase.http.filter.initializers` [!toc]"],[3434,"`hbase.http.max.threads` [!toc]"],[10101,"`hbase.http.max.threads` [!toc]"],[3435,"`hbase.http.metrics.servlets` [!toc]"],[10102,"`hbase.http.metrics.servlets` [!toc]"],[3439,"`hbase.http.staticuser.user` [!toc]"],[10106,"`hbase.http.staticuser.user` [!toc]"],[3370,"`hbase.ipc.client.fallback-to-simple-auth-allowed` [!toc]"],[10037,"`hbase.ipc.client.fallback-to-simple-auth-allowed` [!toc]"],[8030,"`hbase.ipc.client.tcpnodelay = true`"],[13484,"`hbase.ipc.client.tcpnodelay = true`"],[3359,"`hbase.ipc.client.tcpnodelay` [!toc]"],[10026,"`hbase.ipc.client.tcpnodelay` [!toc]"],[3249,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.handler.factor` [!toc]"],[9916,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.handler.factor` [!toc]"],[3250,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.read.ratio` [!toc]"],[9917,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.read.ratio` [!toc]"],[3251,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.scan.ratio` [!toc]"],[9918,"`hbase.ipc.server.callqueue.scan.ratio` [!toc]"],[3371