as a sparse set of rows, they are physically stored by column family.\nA new column qualifier (column\\_family:column\\_qualifier) can be added to an existing column family at any time."],[2313,"Although contributors have their own checklist for verifications, the following items are usually used for voting on release candidates."],[17175,"Although contributors have their own checklist for verifications, the following items are usually used for voting on release candidates."],[7046,"Although not required, if sourcezkcluster is not set, SyncTable will connect to local HBase\ncluster for both source and target, which does not give any meaningful result."],[16225,"Although not required, if sourcezkcluster is not set, SyncTable will connect to local HBase\ncluster for both source and target, which does not give any meaningful result."],[1075,"Although region splitting is still supported, for optimal performance it should be disabled, either by setting explicitly `DisabledRegionSplitPolicy` or by setting `ConstantSizeRegionSplitPolicy` and very large max region size. You will have to increase to a very large number store's blocking file (`hbase.hstore.blockingStoreFiles`) as well. There is a sanity check on table/column family configuration in case of FIFO compaction and minimum value for number of blocking file is 1000."],[14638,"Although region splitting is still supported, for optimal performance it should be disabled, either by setting explicitly `DisabledRegionSplitPolicy` or by setting `ConstantSizeRegionSplitPolicy` and very large max region size. You will have to increase to a very large number store's blocking file (`hbase.hstore.blockingStoreFiles`) as well. There is a sanity check on table/column family configuration in case of FIFO compaction and minimum value for number of blocking file is 1000."],[1236,"Although splitting the region is a local decision made by the RegionServer, the split process itself must coordinate with many actors. The RegionServer notifies the Master before and after the split, updates the `.META.` table so that clients can discover the new daughter regions, and rearranges the directory structure and data files in HDFS. Splitting is a multi-task process. To enable rollback in case of an error, the RegionServer keeps an in-memory journal about the execution state. The steps taken by the RegionServer to execute the split are illustrated in the \"RegionServer Split Process\" schema below. Each step is labeled with its step number. Actions from RegionServers or Master are shown in red, while actions from the clients are shown in green."],[14220,"Although splitting the region is a local decision made by the RegionServer, the split process itself must coordinate with many actors. The RegionServer notifies the Master before and after the split, updates the `.META.` table so that clients can discover the new daughter regions, and rearranges the directory structure and data files in HDFS. Splitting is a multi-task process. To enable rollback in case of an error, the RegionServer keeps an in-memory journal about the execution state. The steps taken by the RegionServer to execute the split are illustrated in the \"RegionServer Split Process\" schema below. Each step is labeled with its step number. Actions from RegionServers or Master are shown in red, while actions from the clients are shown in green."],[305,"Although the `importtsv` tool is useful in many cases, advanced users may want to generate data programmatically, or import data from other formats. To get started doing so, dig into `ImportTsv.java` and check the JavaDoc for HFileOutputFormat."],[14650,"Although the `importtsv` tool is useful in many cases, advanced users may want to generate data programmatically, or import data from other formats. To get started doing so, dig into `ImportTsv.java` and check the JavaDoc for HFileOutputFormat."],[6069,"Although the framework currently allows one HBase table as input to a MapReduce job, other HBase ta