, and is replacing MapReduce in many use cases."],[8803,"Apache Thrift is a cross-platform, cross-language development framework. HBase includes a Thrift API and filter language. The Thrift API relies on client and server processes."],[9791,"Apache ZooKeeper also supports SSL/TLS client connections to encrypt the data in transmission. This is particularly\nuseful when the ZooKeeper ensemble is running on a host different from HBase and data has to be sent\nover the wire."],[17656,"Apache ZooKeeper also supports SSL/TLS client connections to encrypt the data in transmission. This is particularly\nuseful when the ZooKeeper ensemble is running on a host different from HBase and data has to be sent\nover the wire."],[4824,"Apart from downloading HBase, this procedure should take less than 10 minutes."],[11784,"Apart from downloading HBase, this procedure should take less than 10 minutes."],[9061,"Apart from load, we can see that the system is using almost all its available RAM but most of it is used for the OS cache (which is good). The swap only has a few KBs in it and this is wanted, high numbers would indicate swapping activity which is the nemesis of performance of Java systems. Another way to detect swapping is when the load average goes through the roof (although this could also be caused by things like a dying disk, among others)."],[15929,"Apart from load, we can see that the system is using almost all its available RAM but most of it is used for the OS cache (which is good). The swap only has a few KBs in it and this is wanted, high numbers would indicate swapping activity which is the nemesis of performance of Java systems. Another way to detect swapping is when the load average goes through the roof (although this could also be caused by things like a dying disk, among others)."],[1143,"Apart from the cache implementation itself, you can set some general configuration options to control how the cache performs. See CacheConfig. After setting any of these optio