ecial internal handling of MOBs\nto maintain performance, consistency, and low operational overhead. MOB support is\nprovided by the work done in HBASE-11339.\nTo take advantage of MOB, you need to use HFile version 3. Optionally,\nconfigure the MOB file reader's cache settings for each RegionServer (see\nConfigure the MOB Cache), then configure specific columns to hold MOB data.\nClient code does not need to change to take advantage of HBase MOB support. The\nfeature is transparent to the client."],[7102,"Data generated via MapReduce is often created with file permissions that are not compatible with the running HBase process. Assuming you're running HDFS with permissions enabled, those permissions will need to be updated before you run CompleteBulkLoad."],[16281,"Data generated via MapReduce is often created with file permissions that are not compatible with the running HBase process. Assuming you're running HDFS with permissions enabled, those permissions will need to be updated before you run CompleteBulkLoad."],[2331,"Data Generation"],[11563,"Data Generation"],[5826,"Data index — version 2 multi-level block index, consisting of:"],[18762,"Data index — version 2 multi-level block index, consisting of:"],[5881,"Data index offset (long)"],[18817,"Data index offset (long)"],[9532,"Data Locality"],[10196,"Data Locality"],[4226,"Data Model"],[10284,"Data Model"],[4251,"Data Model Operations"],[10308,"Data Model Operations"],[2367,"Data Size"],[18114,"Data Size"],[7852,"Data size and data arrival rate"],[13306,"Data size and data arrival rate"],[519,"Data values over than the MOB threshold show up stored in non-MOB hfiles"],[10733,"Data values over than the MOB threshold show up stored in non-MOB hfiles"],[1068,"Data which can be kept entirely in a a block cache (RAM/SSD). No need for compaction of a raw data at all."],[14631,"Data which can be kept entirely in a a block cache (RAM/SSD). No need for compaction of a raw data at all."],[6957,"DataBlockEncoding validati