edRead` in hbase-2.4.0 — had clients read the primary and if no response after a configurable amount of time had elapsed, it would start up reads against the replicas. Starting from hbase-2.4.12(and all higher minor versions), with client-side `LoadBalance` mode, clients load balance META scan requests across all META replica regions, including the primary META region. In case of exceptions such as NotServingRegionException, it will fall back on the primary META region."],[3008,"HBase-2.4.x"],[12045,"HBase-2.4.x"],[2975,"HBase-2.5.x"],[12012,"HBase-2.5.x"],[2976,"HBase-2.6.x"],[12013,"HBase-2.6.x"],[7475,"HBASE-21926 introduced a new servlet that\nsupports integrated, on-demand profiling via the\nAsync Profiler project."],[15833,"HBASE-21926 introduced a new servlet that\nsupports integrated, on-demand profiling via the\nAsync Profiler project."],[6602,"HBASE-22978 introduces maintaining an in-memory ring buffer of requests that were judged to be too slow in addition to the responseTooSlow logging. The in-memory representation can be complete. There is some chance a high rate of requests will cause information on other interesting requests to be overwritten before it can be read. This is an acceptable trade off."],[16500,"HBASE-22978 introduces maintaining an in-memory ring buffer of requests that were judged to be too slow in addition to the responseTooSlow logging. The in-memory representation can be complete. There is some chance a high rate of requests will cause information on other interesting requests to be overwritten before it can be read. This is an acceptable trade off."],[1224,"HBASE-27999 implements the cache aware load balancer, which adds to the load balancer the ability to consider the cache allocation of each region on region servers when calculating a new assignment plan, using the region/region server cache allocation information reported by region servers to calculate the percentage of HFiles cached for each region on the hosting server. This information is then used by the balancer as a factor when deciding on an optimal, new assignment plan."],[14208,"HBASE-27999 implements the cache aware load balancer, which adds to the load balancer the ability to consider the cache allocation of each region on region servers when calculating a new assignment plan, using the region/region server cache allocation information reported by region servers to calculate the percentage of HFiles cached for each region on the hosting server. This information is then used by the balancer as a factor when deciding on an optimal, new assignment plan."],[1192,"HBASE-28463 introduced time based priority for blocks in BucketCache. It allows for defining an age threshold at individual column families' configuration, whereby blocks older than this configured threshold would be targeted first for eviction."],[14176,"HBASE-28463 introduced time based priority for blocks in BucketCache. It allows for defining an age threshold at individual column families' configuration, whereby blocks older than this configured threshold would be targeted first for eviction."],[7815,"HBASE-4811 implements an API to scan a table\nor a range within a table in reverse, reducing the need to optimize your schema for forward or\nreverse scanning. This feature is available in HBase 0.98 and later. See\nScan.setReversed()\nfor more information."],[7888,"HBASE-4811 implements an API to scan a table\nor a range within a table in reverse, reducing the need to optimize your schema for forward or\nreverse scanning. This feature is available in HBase 0.98 and later. See\nScan.setReversed()\nfor more information."],[13269,"HBASE-4811 implements an API to scan a table\nor a range within a table in reverse, reducing the need to optimize your schema for forward or\nreverse scanning. This feature is available in HBase 0.98 and later. See\nScan.setReversed()\nfor more information."],[13342,"HBASE-4811 implements an API to scan a table\nor a range within a table in reverse, 