 restored does not exist in the target environment, it will be\nautomatically created during the restore operation.\nHBASE-25707"],[912,"If the number of StoreFiles in this set (not the size of the StoreFiles) is fewer than `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` or more than `hbase.hstore.compaction.max`, take it out of consideration."],[14475,"If the number of StoreFiles in this set (not the size of the StoreFiles) is fewer than `hbase.hstore.compaction.min` or more than `hbase.hstore.compaction.max`, take it out of consideration."],[2511,"If the person making the commit is the contributor, leave off the '(\\<contributor>)' element."],[17752,"If the person making the commit is the contributor, leave off the '(\\<contributor>)' element."],[748,"If the region assignment is still valid (i.e., if the RegionServer is still online) then the assignment is kept."],[14311,"If the region assignment is still valid (i.e., if the RegionServer is still online) then the assignment is kept."],[301,"If the region boundaries have changed during the course of bulk load preparation, or between the preparation and completion steps, the `completebulkload` utility will automatically split the data files into pieces corresponding to the new boundaries. This process is not optimally efficient, so users should take care to minimize the delay between preparing a bulk load and importing it into the cluster, especially if other clients are simultaneously loading data through other means."],[14646,"If the region boundaries have changed during the course of bulk load preparation, or between the preparation and completion steps, the `completebulkload` utility will automatically split the data files into pieces corresponding to the new boundaries. This process is not optimally efficient, so users should take care to minimize the delay between preparing a bulk load and importing it into the cluster, especially if other clients are simultaneously loading data through other means."],[3928,"If the regions are 