rovides details about Admin APIs:"],[6518,"The active, initialized Master exposes numeric switch-state gauges under\n`Hadoop:service=HBase,name=Master,sub=Server`. A value of `1` means enabled and\n`0` means disabled. The gauges are absent on backup Masters and before the Master\nis initialized.\nEnabled states indicate that an operation is permitted, rather than that it is\ncurrently running."],[16416,"The active, initialized Master exposes numeric switch-state gauges under\n`Hadoop:service=HBase,name=Master,sub=Server`. A value of `1` means enabled and\n`0` means disabled. The gauges are absent on backup Masters and before the Master\nis initialized.\nEnabled states indicate that an operation is permitted, rather than that it is\ncurrently running."],[6406,"The actual date of last successful edit shipment."],[16720,"The actual date of last successful edit shipment."],[1489,"The admin notices that the following line in the command output corresponds with the *green\\_set* backup that needs to be restored:"],[15026,"The admin notices that the following line in the command output corresponds with the *green\\_set* backup that needs to be restored:"],[1490,"The admin restores green\\_set invoking the backup ID and the -overwrite option. The -overwrite option truncates all existing data\nin the destination and populates the tables with data from the backup dataset. Without this flag, the backup data is appended to the\nexisting data in the destination. In this case, the admin decides to overwrite the data because it is corrupted."],[15027,"The admin restores green\\_set invoking the backup ID and the -overwrite option. The -overwrite option truncates all existing data\nin the destination and populates the tables with data from the backup dataset. Without this flag, the backup data is appended to the\nexisting data in the destination. In this case, the admin decides to overwrite the data because it is corrupted."],[1488,"The admin scans the list to see which backup was 