' state.\nWhile in this 'open' state you can check out what you've published to make sure all is good.\nTo do this, log in to Apache's Nexus at repository.apache.org using your Apache ID.\nFind your artifacts in the staging repository. Click on 'Staging Repositories' and look for a new one ending in \"hbase\" with a status of 'Open', select it.\nUse the tree view to expand the list of repository contents and inspect if the artifacts you expect are present. Check the POMs.\nAs long as the staging repo is open you can re-upload if something is missing or built incorrectly."],[232,"The AssignmentManager (AM) in HBase Master manages assignment of Regions over a cluster of RegionServers."],[486,"The authority part *server1:16020,server2:16020,server3:16020* specifies the bootstrap nodes and their rpc ports, i.e, the configuration value for *hbase.client.bootstrap.servers* in the past."],[14041,"The authority part *server1:16020,server2:16020,server3:16020* specifies the bootstrap nodes and their rpc ports, i.e, the configuration value for *hbase.client.bootstrap.servers* in the past."],[488,"The authority part *zk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181* is the zk quorum, i.e, the configuration value for *hbase.zookeeper.quorum&#x2A; in the past. The path part */hbase* is the znode parent, i.e, the configuration value for *zookeeper.znode.parent* in the past."],[14043,"The authority part *zk1:2181,zk2:2181,zk3:2181* is the zk quorum, i.e, the configuration value for *hbase.zookeeper.quorum&#x2A; in the past. The path part */hbase* is the znode parent, i.e, the configuration value for *zookeeper.znode.parent* in the past."],[6801,"The authors of the rsgroup feature, the Yahoo! HBase Engineering team, have been running it on their grid for a good while now and have come up with a few best practices informed by their experience."],[16952,"The authors of the rsgroup feature, the Yahoo! HBase Engineering team, have been running it on their grid for a good while now and have come up with a few best practices informed by their experience."],[2627,"The available codec implementation options are:"],[18525,"The available codec implementation options are:"],[7368,"The average false positive rate for bloom filters. Folding is used to maintain the false positive rate. Expressed as a decimal representation of a percentage."],[15733,"The average false positive rate for bloom filters. Folding is used to maintain the false positive rate. Expressed as a decimal representation of a percentage."],[5872,"The average key length in the file (int)"],[18808,"The average key length in the file (int)"],[5874,"The average value length in the file (int)"],[18810,"The average value length in the file (int)"],[9464,"The backing implementation of HBase's tracing features was updated from Apache HTrace 3 to HTrace 4, which includes several breaking changes. While HTrace 3 and 4 can coexist in the same runtime, they will not integrate with each other, leading to disjoint trace information."],[12980,"The backing implementation of HBase's tracing features was updated from Apache HTrace 3 to HTrace 4, which includes several breaking changes. While HTrace 3 and 4 can coexist in the same runtime, they will not integrate with each other, leading to disjoint trace information."],[1460,"The backup and restore feature includes both required and optional configuration keys."],[14997,"The backup and restore feature includes both required and optional configuration keys."],[1662,"The backup and restore feature introduces new terminology which can be used to understand how control flows through the\nsystem."],[14902,"The backup and restore feature introduces new terminology which can be used to understand how control flows through the\nsystem."],[1652,"The backup and restore feature supplements the HBase Replication feature. While HBase replication is ideal for\ncreating \"hot\" copies of the data (where the replicated data is immediately available for query), the backup and\nrestore feature i