e block index in version 1 is that it does not provide the compressed size of a block, which turns out to be necessary for decompression.\nTherefore, the HFile reader has to infer this compressed size from the offset difference between blocks.\nWe fix this limitation in version 2, where we store on-disk block size instead of uncompressed size, and get uncompressed size from the block header."],[5985,"The number of flushes carried by the pipeline is monitored so as to fit within the bounds of memstore sizing\nbut you can also set a maximum on the number of flushes total by setting\n*hbase.hregion.compacting.pipeline.segments.limit*. Default is 2."],[14852,"The number of flushes carried by the pipeline is monitored so as to fit within the bounds of memstore sizing\nbut you can also set a maximum on the number of flushes total by setting\n*hbase.hregion.compacting.pipeline.segments.limit*. Default is 2."],[5478,"The number of iterations"],[17767,"The number of iterations"],[5892,"The number of levels in the data block index (int)"],[18828,"The number of levels in the data block index (int)"],[1061,"The number of new stripes to create when splitting a stripe. The default is 2, which is appropriate for most cases. For non-uniform row keys, you can experiment with increasing the number to 3 or 4, to isolate the arriving updates into narrower slice of the region without additional splits being required."],[14624,"The number of new stripes to create when splitting a stripe. The default is 2, which is appropriate for most cases. For non-uniform row keys, you can experiment with increasing the number to 3 or 4, to isolate the arriving updates into narrower slice of the region without additional splits being required."],[6377,"The number of region servers a given region server should attempt to failover simultaneously."],[16691,"The number of region servers a given region server should attempt to failover simultaneously."],[1057,"The number of stripes to create when stripe com